From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 99992: look for the client across the whole MLD, not one BSS

9999 taught agent_set_sta_resp() to compare the requested MLD address against
s->mld_macaddr, which was necessary and not sufficient: it still only searched
ap->stalist for the single AP the source BSSID resolved to. An MLO client is
held under the address of the affiliated link it associated on, and its links
sit on different affiliated APs of the same MLD, so the search misses whenever
the client came up on a link other than the one named.

Measured on hardware 2026-08-03, client on 4g with the request naming
ap-mld-1:

	agent_set_sta_resp: sta: 7a:6f:6d:db:82:92 not found

	map.agent status:
	  AP mld=ap-mld-1  stations ['9e:fe:2e:69:98:59']   aff=True mld=7a:6f:...
	  AP mld=ap-mld-1  stations ['3a:c4:83:fd:39:bf']   aff=True mld=7a:6f:...
	  AP mld=ap-mld-1  stations []                      <- searched this one

The client was in the model, correctly attributed, on an AP the search never
looked at. The controller addresses a client by its MLD address and an MLD
BSS; the MLD is therefore the unit to search, and this makes it so.

Same defect class as 9997, 9998 and 9999 - the fifth place today where code
written for one link per BSS meets an entity that has several.

Also removed while here: the "not found" branch tested a `found` flag that was
never reset between iterations of the STA loop, so with more than one station
in the request every station after the first match was silently treated as
found. It is an if/else on the lookup result now. num_sta is 1 in every
request seen so far, which is why this never showed.
--- a/src/agent_map.c
+++ b/src/agent_map.c
@@ -4598,51 +4598,86 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
+/* An MLO client is held under the address of the affiliated link it associated
+ * on, and its links are spread over the affiliated APs of one MLD. A request
+ * names the client by its MLD address and one BSS, so searching only that BSS
+ * finds nothing whenever the client came up on a different link of the same
+ * MLD. The MLD is the unit the controller addresses; make it the unit we
+ * search. */
+static struct sta *ap_find_sta(struct netif_ap *ap, uint8_t *mac)
+{
+	struct sta *s = NULL;
+
+	list_for_each_entry(s, &ap->stalist, list) {
+		if (!memcmp(s->macaddr, mac, 6))
+			return s;
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+		if (s->is_affiliated_sta && !memcmp(s->mld_macaddr, mac, 6))
+			return s;
+#endif
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+static struct sta *mld_find_sta(struct agent *a, struct netif_ap *ap, uint8_t *mac)
+{
+	struct sta *s;
+
+	s = ap_find_sta(ap, mac);
+	if (s)
+		return s;
+
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+	if (ap->is_affiliated_ap && ap->mld_ifname[0]) {
+		struct wifi_radio_element *re = NULL;
+
+		list_for_each_entry(re, &a->radiolist, list) {
+			struct netif_ap *o = NULL;
+
+			list_for_each_entry(o, &re->aplist, list) {
+				if (o == ap || !o->is_affiliated_ap)
+					continue;
+				if (strncmp(o->mld_ifname, ap->mld_ifname,
+					    sizeof(o->mld_ifname)))
+					continue;
+
+				s = ap_find_sta(o, mac);
+				if (s)
+					return s;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
